From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] boot: print the banner and errors only

At 115 200 baud every character on the console costs 87 us, and U-Boot
printed about 1 300 of them on each boot: the DRAM, driver model and MMC
summaries, the environment source, "N bytes read", four lines per FIT
image, the relocation lines and "Starting kernel". They are debug() now;
errors are not touched, and a FIT hash failure names the image, since
the line before it is gone. image-fit.c and image.c are also built into
mkimage, which keeps their output.

---
